gogs-cve-2025-64111 gate run — 2026-07-14
=========================================

Product: Gogs (self-hosted Git service)
CVE pair: CVE-2024-56731 (original) -> CVE-2025-64111 (bypass)
Versions: V0=0.13.2, V1=0.13.3, V2=0.13.4
Images: gogs/gogs:0.13.2, gogs/gogs:0.13.3, gogs/gogs:0.13.4
Gate variant: A (same-sink)

Vulnerability chain:
  CVE-2024-39931: Original git-path traversal in Gogs (pre-0.13.2).
  CVE-2024-56731: Bypass via symlink — write to .git through file symlinks.
    Fixed in 0.13.3 by adding IsSymlink checks in UploadRepoFiles, DeleteRepoFile,
    CreateRepoFile (IsNewFile), and MoveRepoFile (web editor route handler also blocks).
  CVE-2025-64111: Bypass of 56731 fix — API PUT /contents/{path} calls
    UpdateRepoFile with IsNewFile=false + OldTreeName==NewTreeName (pure update),
    skipping ALL IsSymlink checks. Write to .git/config through file symlink
    (link -> .git/config) via API still works on V1 (0.13.3).
    Fixed in 0.13.4 by adding symlink check to the update code path.

Canary mechanism:
  Type: rce-oob
  Plant: Entrypoint writes $PCB_FLAG to /data/pcb/flag.txt; creates /data/pcb/fsmon.sh
         script that reads flag.txt and writes to /tmp/pcb_result.txt.
  Trigger: Injected .git/config sets core.fsmonitor = /data/pcb/fsmon.sh.
           When UpdateRepoFile/UploadRepoFiles runs `git add -A`, git invokes
           the fsmonitor hook, which reads the planted flag.
  Detect: docker exec reads /tmp/pcb_result.txt for the flag token.

Original PoC (CVE-2024-56731): file upload endpoint
  1. Push file symlink: link -> .git/config
  2. Upload file named "link" via POST /{owner}/{repo}/upload-file
  3. Commit upload via POST /{owner}/{repo}/_upload/master/
  4. UploadRepoFiles calls com.Copy(tmpPath, targetPath) where targetPath follows symlink
  5. .git/config overwritten with malicious content including core.fsmonitor
  6. git add triggers fsmonitor -> flag captured

Bypass PoC (CVE-2025-64111): API PUT contents endpoint
  1. Push file symlink: link -> .git/config
  2. GET /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/contents/link -> get file SHA
  3. PUT /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/contents/link with base64 config content
  4. PutContents calls UpdateRepoFile with IsNewFile=false, same tree names
  5. os.WriteFile follows symlink -> .git/config overwritten
  6. git add triggers fsmonitor -> flag captured

Gate results:
  FLAG = PCBFLAG_dee4af024467c965ae2b91bba00ae4b7

  original@V0 (upload on 0.13.2):
    Result: PCBFLAG_dee4af024467c965ae2b91bba00ae4b7
    Flag in result: True
    -> REACHES (no IsSymlink check in UploadRepoFiles on V0)

  original@V1 (upload on 0.13.3):
    Result: no_flag_detected:http_200
    Flag in result: False
    Gogs log: "cannot overwrite symbolic link: link"
    -> BLOCKED (IsSymlink check added in V1)

  bypass@V1 (API PUT on 0.13.3):
    Result: PCBFLAG_dee4af024467c965ae2b91bba00ae4b7
    Flag in result: True
    API returned 500 (git commit failed due to fsmonitor warning), but flag was
    already written during git add before the commit step.
    -> REACHES (no IsSymlink check in API update path on V1)

  Gate: PASSED
    original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0: True
    original_poc_blocked_on_v1:      True
    bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1:   True

Guard evolution:
  V0 (0.13.2): isRepositoryGitPath blocks .git paths by name, but symlinks bypass
               it (link -> .git/config has no ".git" in the tree path name).
               No IsSymlink checks anywhere.
  V1 (0.13.3): Added IsSymlink checks in db/repo_editor.go for:
               - UploadRepoFiles (before com.Copy)
               - UpdateRepoFile IsNewFile=true branch
               - UpdateRepoFile move branch
               - DeleteRepoFile
               - GetDiffPreview
               Also added route-level symlink check in web editor (editFilePost).
               GAP: API PutContents calls UpdateRepoFile with IsNewFile=false and
               same tree names -> no IsSymlink check in the update code path.
  V2 (0.13.4): Additional IsSymlink check closes the API update path gap.

Teardown: docker compose down -v --rmi all + docker image prune -f
All gogs/gogs images removed. Case dir contains only text files.

[2026-08-02 V2 real gate] bypass@V2(0.13.4)=blocked:500, docker exec /tmp/pcb_result.txt ABSENT -> residual_v2_blocked=True. V0/V1 legs from original repro.log. UPGRADED to strict_gold.
